{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545404-mtaw-dark-eras-origins-of-orders-when-orders-spread-on-world-tome-of-pentacle","id":1545404,"title":"[MtAw Dark Eras] Origins of Orders - WHEN Orders spread on World? [Tome of Pentacle]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-05T13:39:35-08:00","id":1545404,"title":"[MtAw Dark Eras] Origins of Orders - WHEN Orders spread on World? [Tome of Pentacle]","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">So let\u2019s return from 2E point of view to idea of Orders cultural exchange \u2013 and they export over the Fallen World. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1544190-mtaw-dark-eras-origins-of-orders-why-so-late-tome-of-pentacle\">Remembering that \u2018Proto-Diamond\u2019 Orders are based from Darshanas in Rome circa 3<sup>rd</sup> century BCE</a> \u2013 <b>When they could influx local mage cultures of Far East, Africa, and alike?</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Looking over Rome\u2019s own timeline:</span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Africa</b> \u2013 Punic Wars ( 264 till 146 BCE ) with Carthage would lead Darshanas to the Norther Africa, with Carthage and Egypt in just 3<sup>rd</sup> century. Creating Mouseion in Library of Alexandria as Keepers of the World headquartering 295 BCE is best example. </span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Asia, West &amp; Central </b>\u2013 From times of Alexander Empire, Persian and Indian mages were influenced with Darshanas ideas - so they would join 'Proto-Diamond\u2019 as <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chronology_of_the_expedition_of_Alexander_the_Great_into_Asia\" target=\"_blank\">early as 330s BCE, following Alexander expeditions into Asia</a>. ( Rome had small but existing community of Indian emigrants already in Roman Empire times, probably earlier even. )</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Americas </b>\u2013 <b>Tome of Pentacle</b> mentioned that first Vikings mages, already in Diamond, come to modern Canada in 1021 CE. Adamantine Arrow dogma strongly resonates with Native American supernal traditions.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Australia </b>\u2013 I <i>suspect </i>\u2018last found continent\u2019 did not have Diamond mages before any contacts with Aboriginal propel of European colonists in 17<sup>th</sup> century?</span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The biggest question for me is..</span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>East Asia</b> ( Far East ) \u2013 <b>China and Japan</b> \u2013 They clearly would have vibrant preDiamond Darshana cults traditions. But when</span> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">'Proto-Diamond\u2019</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">would \u2018show up on their doorsteps\u2019? When they tradition would intermixed with Diamond Orders dogmas? ToP points that founding of Nalanda, first university in Magadha, India in 427 CE is spreading Diamond lore \u2013 but it sounds VERY late to me. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sino-Roman_relations\" target=\"_blank\">Some history scholars points to evidents of first China-Rome relation as early as 1<sup>st</sup> century CE</a> \u2013 with \u2018Diamond almost ready\u2019 then, I do not see reason why it should be not time for propagating Orders in this region at this time.</span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">EDIT: Topic analysis below points </span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Six_Dynasties\" target=\"_blank\">China's Six Dynasties</a> ( 220 CE \u2013 589CE ) from it's start - I still would see starts for circa 220 BCE, would already have basis of (proto)Diamond in themselves. \ud83d\ude2e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-07-2024, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-05T17:28:10-08:00","id":1545418,"title":"","content":"I really think you're focusing heavily on the idea of the Orders arising from around Rome specifically, and that's just not the case.<br /> <br /> Like, I find it super weird to say &quot;Indian mages were influenced with Darshanas ideas&quot; when <i>Darshana is a Sanskrit word!!!</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-05T21:16:20-08:00","id":1545432,"title":"","content":"It's like... <b><i>Idea</i></b> of Darshana as 'universal cults around the world' may come from India and their Caste system traditions - but the PUSH for the organizing Orders as global powers is much more logical to came from Empires - Alexander Greece and then Rome. In local Indian cults there is no real reason for 'self reflecting' that they are all the same and should join 'great Orders federation', so to speak.<br /> <br /> ( You may point this early divides over 'and we are different people, we and our neighborhors' - as Unity Exarch early workings - but remember that mages would not understand of Iron Seals till early Middle Ages. It's Fallen World not without reason )<br /> <br /> India in 3rd to 1st century BCE is very much split on very small kingdoms. There is no need for 'universal powers' in that region. And, as pointed by <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Tome of Pentacle</b> and modern history research - cultural exchange was rather constant with Rome and India subcontinent in that time.<br /> <br /> On the other hand - once <b><i>Adamantine Arrows</i></b> Darshana protoOrder is established within Roman Legion - it's logical it will spread from there, whenever Romans will show up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-06-2024, 12:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-06T08:35:32-08:00","id":1545468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545404-mtaw-dark-eras-origins-of-orders-when-orders-spread-on-world-tome-of-pentacle?p=1545432#post1545432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's like... <b><i>Idea</i></b> of Darshana as 'universal cults around the world' may come from India and their Caste system traditions - but the PUSH for the organizing Orders as global powers is much more logical to came from Empires - Alexander Greece and then Rome. In local Indian cults there is no real reason for 'self reflecting' that they are all the same and should join 'great Orders federation', so to speak.<br /> <br /> ( You may point this early divides over 'and we are different people, we and our neighborhors' - as Unity Exarch early workings - but remember that mages would not understand of Iron Seals till early Middle Ages. It's Fallen World not without reason )<br /> <br /> India in 3rd to 1st century BCE is very much split on very small kingdoms. There is no need for 'universal powers' in that region. And, as pointed by <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Tome of Pentacle</b> and modern history research - cultural exchange was rather constant with Rome and India subcontinent in that time.<br /> <br /> On the other hand - once <b><i>Adamantine Arrows</i></b> Darshana protoOrder is established within Roman Legion - it's logical it will spread from there, whenever Romans will show up.</div> </div> </div> </div>This runs on the assumption that the Awakened are bound to human methods of connectivity that empires facilitate, going right down to the roads, messengers, and traders.<br /> <br /> The presence of the Mastigos and every mage's ready access to the Astral obviates this train of thought. The Diamond was running ahead of Rome by centuries, particularly once the archetypalism of the nascent Diamond made it clear how the Great Cults could intgrate.<br /> <br /> And even if we assume empire was a major influence on how the Diamond expanded... you're still ignoring how the Mauryan Empire created a whole ass gateway for the Diamond into the East.<br /> <br /> That said, your question on when the Fang Shih joined is a good one, when I get the books after work, I can see how much of an answer there is for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-07-2024, 10:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-06T12:29:15-08:00","id":1545485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545404-mtaw-dark-eras-origins-of-orders-when-orders-spread-on-world-tome-of-pentacle?p=1545432#post1545432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's like... <b><i>Idea</i></b> of Darshana as 'universal cults around the world' may come from India and their Caste system traditions - but the PUSH for the organizing Orders as global powers is much more logical to came from Empires - Alexander Greece and then Rome. In local Indian cults there is no real reason for 'self reflecting' that they are all the same and should join 'great Orders federation', so to speak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting aside everything to do with how syncretic the Hellenistic World was, how much of Iranian and Indian culture was drawn over to the Mediterranean and Greek culture in turn (have a look into Greco-Buddhism some time)...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">India in 3rd to 1st century BCE is very much split on very small kingdoms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chandragupta is called out by name in Tome of the Pentacle. This-<br /> <img width=\"900\" height=\"841\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2c/Maurya_Empire%2C_c.250_BCE_2.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2c/Maurya_Empire%2C_c.250_BCE_2.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2c/Maurya_Empire%2C_c.250_BCE_2.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> is what the empire he founded looked like right dab in the middle of the period you're calling out.<br /> <br /> Never mind the extent to &quot;split into lots of smaller states&quot; is irrelevant to the capacity for common cultural and intellectual spheres when we are also talking about <i>ancient Greece</i>.<br /> <br /> (The Greco-Bactrians up there in the top left are another kingdom left behind from the Alexandrian empire. They heavily featured syncretism of Greek, Persian, and Indian culture at their time, and remained a major hub of trade and communication between those spheres for centuries).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 11-06-2024, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-06T14:03:03-08:00","id":1545490,"title":"","content":"There's a relevant sentence in the description of the Consilium Age in <i>TotP</i>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The age of the initial Diamond Orders riding the Roman Empire and Six Dynasties out ward... </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-06T15:52:05-08:00","id":1545496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545404-mtaw-dark-eras-origins-of-orders-when-orders-spread-on-world-tome-of-pentacle?p=1545468#post1545468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This runs on the assumption that the Awakened are bound to human methods of connectivity that empires facilitate, going right down to the roads, messengers, and traders.<br /> <br /> The presence of the Mastigos and every mage's ready access to the Astral obviates this train of thought. The Diamond was running ahead of Rome by centuries, particularly once the archetypalism of the nascent Diamond made it clear how the Great Cults could intgrate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would note that, as the books depict it, while following the lines of human cultural drift is not strictly necessary, it is ultimately a lot more convenient and can carry a lot more bulk than having to do everything with their magic does. The Diamond Orders hold themselves somewhat apart from Sleeper society, but much of their infrastructure is still embedded in its institutions, and it would appear that it's generally been easier to move that along incrementally (and then use the base it establishes to build power and knowledge to incentivize Nameless into their ranks) than to build from scratch.<br /> <br /> And indeed, in its time, Rome <i>is</i> supposed to have played a major part in this. That's been consistent in depictions of Awakened history ever since Guardians of the Veil came out.<br /> <br /> It's just that the formation of the proto-Orders precedes that within a different network of interconnected people. The infrastructure of meeting points for artists, intellectuals, merchants, and aristocrats found in the Hellenistic world, wherein Greeks, Persians, Egyptians, and Indians (and many other people besides) is also fertile ground for Awakened of different Great Cults to encounter one another at a large enough scale to recognise the commonality of the schools forming within them, and the forums for establishing common society that will build those schools into Orders distanced from their differing cultural backgrounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-06T19:54:00-08:00","id":1545512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545404-mtaw-dark-eras-origins-of-orders-when-orders-spread-on-world-tome-of-pentacle?p=1545490#post1545490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a relevant sentence in the description of the Consilium Age in [I]TotP[/IThe age of the initial Diamond Orders riding the Roman Empire and Six Dynasties out ward...</div> </div> </div> </div>Six Dynasties? Interesting. Did they mean the Proxy Dynasties? Or other kingdoms names? \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-06T20:07:14-08:00","id":1545513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545404-mtaw-dark-eras-origins-of-orders-when-orders-spread-on-world-tome-of-pentacle?p=1545512#post1545512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Six Dynasties? Interesting. Did they mean the Proxy Dynasties? Or other kingdoms names? \ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Six_Dynasties\" target=\"_blank\">China</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-06T22:16:14-08:00","id":1545515,"title":"","content":"Okay, so we have TWO Post-Alexandrian empires - <b>Rome </b>and <b>Maurya</b> in India - that help crystalize (proto)Diamond whole 3rd century BCE. ( Three if we take in concept Greco-Bactrians in that area. ) So once this going, from 2nd century onwards - I can easily see <b>China being 'neighbor' to Maurya</b>, spread (proto)Orders further. With local timeline shaping, I would be not surprised that <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Six_Dynasties\" target=\"_blank\">China's Six Dynasties</a>, from the start of those circa 220 BCE would already have basis of (proto)Diamond in themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-07T04:16:42-08:00","id":1545520,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly, <i>Tome of the Pentacle</i> traces the solidifying of the proto-Orders to the Spring and Autumn period and the Hundred Schools of Thought. So by that timeline, it would start with the Eastern Zhou dynasty and then catch the Chen, Liang and Southern Qi dynasties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-07T09:59:14-08:00","id":1545526,"title":"","content":"I would characterise the information provided in the book as conveying that mages of East Asia are within a philosophical basis sophisticated enough to form similar conclusions to the Hellenistic mages as the basis of schools, but the level of warfare and divided boundaries at the time inhibits them from cohering into organizations like Orders.<br /> <br /> Hence, when the Diamond starts spreading outwards, they encounter mages who are already kindred with them (and may have already had some preliminary magical contact), and have an already well established framework and hierarchy to integrate into.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, the order of events still means that a lot of the details take their cues from the Diamond Cradle (even if there are evidently several ways that Chinese concepts and cosmetics got back into the larger Diamond), and this remains a sore spot with some regional mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-07T14:04:21-08:00","id":1545532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545404-mtaw-dark-eras-origins-of-orders-when-orders-spread-on-world-tome-of-pentacle#post1545404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[/LIST]EDIT: Topic analysis below points <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Six_Dynasties\" target=\"_blank\">China's Six Dynasties</a> ( 220 BCE \u2013 589CE ) from it's start in circa 220 BCE, would already have basis of (proto)Diamond in themselves. \ud83d\ude2e</div> </div> </div> </div>Slight correction. It's 220<b>CE</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-07T14:47:04-08:00","id":1545533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545404-mtaw-dark-eras-origins-of-orders-when-orders-spread-on-world-tome-of-pentacle?p=1545532#post1545532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slight correction. It's 220<b>CE</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again, later Orders. \ud83d\ude44 I would still posit (proto)Diamond would be in area as end of 3rd century BCE, by trade with 'neighbour' <b>Maurya</b> Empire. But instead of semi-colescent Diamond, they are locally still on Darshana self-reflecting levels of postAlexandrian Hellenistic World, like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> posits.<br /> <br /> After Diamond 'is almost' backed in Rome by the end of 1st century BCE - Orders are starting to coalescent around all the regions. With China-Rome relations more and more prominent from 2nd century CE, the Diamond there takes root.<br /> <br /> At the Diamond finalising <b>Convocation of Alexandria</b> in 265 CE there are already Chinese delegations of proper Orders. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-07T14:58:14-08:00","id":1545534,"title":"","content":"Exploring from <b>China to Japan -</b> I suspect first enterings of Diamond Orders to Japan were done already in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_Japan#Kofun_period_(c._250%E2%80%93538)\" target=\"_blank\">Kofun period ( 250 - 538 CE )</a> from Six Dynasties of China. From Asuka period from 538 AD onward, with Buddhist missionaries from Korea, it would be constant Orders structures in Japan - especially taking in account mentioned before university <i><b>Nalanda</b></i> in India, exporting Awakened lore in and to China, Korea, and Tibet.<br /> <br /> And by this, I think we have Far East Orders spreading cracked. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-07T18:20:38-08:00","id":1545545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545404-mtaw-dark-eras-origins-of-orders-when-orders-spread-on-world-tome-of-pentacle?p=1545533#post1545533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Once again, later Orders. \ud83d\ude44</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the Orders are just plain going to come to some places later than others. What is the objection behind the idea that it takes a while for the Orders to effectively spread to somewhere that is geographically far from their heartland?<br /> <br /> Still, the language of riding the period outwards would be the kind of thing to suggest being present in the core at the beginning of respective periods.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-07T22:24:14-08:00","id":1545552,"title":"","content":"(Late Orders)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545404-mtaw-dark-eras-origins-of-orders-when-orders-spread-on-world-tome-of-pentacle?p=1545545#post1545545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, the Orders are just plain going to come to some places later than others. What is the objection behind the idea that it takes a while for the Orders to effectively spread to somewhere that is geographically far from their heartland?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that I have objection to spreading of Orders taking a bit time around continents. It seems logical.<br /> <br /> I'm more concerned that <b>Tome of Pentacle</b> authors point that Orders took about 600 years (!) 'to cook' into Diamond. Decisive events painted are Alexandrian Empire and creating Mouseion in Library or Alexandria ( circa 295 BCE ) and mentioned 218 BCE meetings of protoArrows with protoSeers - and then, jumps to 250-265 CE with full on inner war of Diamond and Seers inside, ending with Convocation of Alexandria in 265 CE. It's very strange design decision from my POV, especially, taking in account Mastigos and other Mind mages imperative in protoDiamond.<br /> <br /> So, in the end, it's not on the spread of Orders itself - much more how long it took to get Diamond full on Orders in the 'concept'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-07T23:13:21-08:00","id":1545560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545404-mtaw-dark-eras-origins-of-orders-when-orders-spread-on-world-tome-of-pentacle?p=1545552#post1545552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm more concerned that <b>Tome of Pentacle</b> authors point that Orders took about 600 years (!) 'to cook' into Diamond. Decisive events painted are Alexandrian Empire and creating Mouseion in Library or Alexandria ( circa 295 BCE ) and mentioned 218 BCE meetings of protoArrows with protoSeers - and then, jumps to 250-265 CE with full on inner war of Diamond and Seers inside, ending with Convocation of Alexandria in 265 CE. It's very strange design decision from my POV, especially, taking in account Mastigos and other Mind mages imperative in protoDiamond.<br /> <br /> So, in the end, it's not on the spread of Orders itself - much more how long it took to get Diamond full on Orders in the 'concept'.</div> </div> </div> </div>This feels like it betrays some teleological thinking: the Diamond Precept was the culminatory decision that marked the transition from most mages belonging to national Great Cults to the emergence of the Orders as a group with a unified organization not bound to any one country, and the Diamond Precept was not the specific aim of most of the mages whose ideas eventually created it \u2014 even in the modern day the Ladder is still the only one with special investment in the premise of the Diamond as a unified system.<br /> <br /> Barring archmaster meddling retroactively or with extreme foresight that the setting hasn't seen fit to enshrine in the text, nobody in the Chronicles of Darkness sat down and said, &quot;We gotta get the Diamond Precept pieced together this many centuries before Byzantium.&quot; It was an organic development that happened as a bunch of different groups of mages existed in the world during that span of history in their own contexts that put some of them in contact to share findings and debate theory and practice.<br /> <br /> It took over 300 years from the birth of Jesus for Christianity to make the Nicene Creed, and that had the advantage of being a mode of thought corresponding to the teachings of a single geographically limited origin point \u2014 double that for a &quot;distinct minority&quot; of mages to grow their numbers and sort out their policies and allegiances certainly sounds about right, especially considering that 1200 years later in the Opposition Age the first Ministry is noted as a change in the Diamond's enemies from being barely organized to being <i>much</i> better organized.<br /> <br /> It's worth remembering that leaning on the versatility of magic as an argument for mages theoretically being able to accomplish grand goals faster must contend with the fact that most mages have their own priorities and even the chain of tutelage only reduces the number of mages that need to be persuaded to help so much. This is a type of supernatural being whose themes and cultural touchstones lend themselves to hermitage and isolation, and in the age before the printing press and the combustion engine and well after the time that omphalos stones were a resource that means most of them aren't going to be getting together at convention centers or wandering around the Astral hoping to meet with strangers who're amenable to hammering out the Exoteric Tenets or the five precepts of the Hand. Calling a Convocation for the first time was a big event.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-08T08:09:14-08:00","id":1545570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545404-mtaw-dark-eras-origins-of-orders-when-orders-spread-on-world-tome-of-pentacle?p=1545552#post1545552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm more concerned that <b>Tome of Pentacle</b> authors point that Orders took about 600 years (!) 'to cook' into Diamond. Decisive events painted are Alexandrian Empire and creating Mouseion in Library or Alexandria ( circa 295 BCE ) and mentioned 218 BCE meetings of protoArrows with protoSeers - and then, jumps to 250-265 CE with full on inner war of Diamond and Seers inside, ending with Convocation of Alexandria in 265 CE. It's very strange design decision from my POV, especially, taking in account Mastigos and other Mind mages imperative in protoDiamond.<br /> <br /> So, in the end, it's not on the spread of Orders itself - much more how long it took to get Diamond full on Orders in the 'concept'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look at what was introduced to the game by To The Strongest, and consider the motivation behind it. Dave Brookshaw once said that a big motive in Second Edition was to give more depth to the premise of mages as academics by not only examining what they believe, but how and why. The premise of the Diamond Orders emerging out of the conquests of Alexander the Great is hence all about not just their origin, but how to depict the emergence of their beliefs and knowledge in a gradual, messy fashion based on the arduous process of syncretism and debate, lots of ad hoc decisions along the way.<br /> <br /> Dave has training as an archaeologist, he'll have a lot of first hand examples of this kind of thing happening in reality. Rome is only built in a day by a namesake founder figure in stories; the truth is of a few neighbouring villages merging together over the course of a few hundred years.<br /> <br /> Or even look at Roman domination of Italy. One might ask why it takes about two hundred years to just conquer one peninsula (compared to the next two hundred in which the conquer most of the Mediterranean). The answer is because it wasn't the goal and it was starting out from a position that was lacking in a lot of resources, and all along the way they would have kept having attention go to other issues that would have been much more pressing to the ones experiencing them even if they seem insignificant in the grand sweep of history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-08T14:06:42-08:00","id":1545582,"title":"","content":"Having had a chance to look at Tome of the Pentacle again, I notice that it provides a more concrete starting point for when the Orders can acquire more prominence in China, namely the Yellow Turban Rebellion in the mid 180s. In particular, it's in the fact that major crisis provides an opportunity for the Orders to demonstrate their value and gain prominence.<br /> <br /> That in combination with the point that about a century before, attempts to create stronger ties between the Roman Empire and Han Dynasty had been frustrated (which fits with historical consensus during that era). So we're presented with circumstances in which the Awakened of the time actually strive to have the Orders there earlier, and face obstacles to doing so.<br /> <br /> I can imagine that mage historians look at some of the time there and think that if the Qin Dynasty had lasted longer, then it may have provided the bedrock of stability for the local equivalent of schools to fully evolve independently into equivalents of Orders. Or at least proto-Orders; I think the distinction between early Order and darshana is nebulous but largely a matter of increasing refinement of mysticism, ideology, and organisation, while becoming properly defined Order in the modern sense is dependent on mages from multiple cultural spheres coming together and both combining their distinctions and recognising what is universal between them. I think China at the time may have lacked the diversity to fully become something like the Diamond Orders by themselves.<br /> <br /> In any case, there's a logical chain of events to help remove some of the obstacles and create an opportunity for the Orders to become a major player among the Awakened population, and from that to both grow outwards along China's expanding frontiers and, ultimately, become the origin point of what will become a pivotal concept of the Keepers of the Word and then Mysterium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}